Drains 35 type-arg errors across four peripheral modules. Clean on the
FIRST whole-tree run: zero hidden errors revealed, zero follow-up rounds.

That is the interesting result. The three batches so far:

  batch 1  compact                                44 drained,  3 revealed, 2 rounds
  batch 2  taint / sketch / io_boundary           43 drained, 37 revealed, 4 rounds
  batch 3  framework_patterns / finalize /
           supply_chain / profile                 35 drained,  0 revealed, 1 round

The variable is not file count or size -- batch 3 is four files. It is how
POLYMORPHIC the module's own interfaces are. taint.py had a genuine
TaintSource|TaintSink union flowing through read-only helpers, a
type-preserving merge, and one loop variable bound to two element types.
These four modules had re.Pattern, set[str], and serialized-dict payloads:
one defensible answer each, so nothing was being masked.

Usable rule for the rest of the drain: type-arg COUNT does not predict
cost; INTERFACE POLYMORPHISM does.

One near-miss worth recording. `FinalizedMap.nodes: tuple` sits in a
dataclass whose neighbouring fields are list[Symbol] and list[Edge], so
both the name and the context argue for tuple[Symbol, ...]. It is built
from `tuple(ctx.behavior_map.get("nodes", []))` -- the SERIALIZED map's
arrays, i.e. dicts. Annotated tuple[dict[str, Any], ...] after reading the
constructor. Inferring from the name would have been the fourth instance
of the mistake that cost batch 2 three extra rounds: the name tells you
what someone meant, only the construction tells you what is there.

Other measured types, not assumed: re.Pattern[str] / re.Match[str] for the
compiled-pattern fields; list[ValidationViolation] for FinalizeContext.
violations (populated by validate_ir); tuple[str, str, str, str, str] for
_violation_sort_key (five string fields); set[str] for the workspace
package-name collector. profile.py gains a TYPE_CHECKING import for Edge /
Symbol -- no cycle exists, but the runtime import graph stays unchanged for
a module the CLI loads on every invocation.

Baseline ratcheted 992 -> 957.

